Updated useState implementation in the Gratuity component. Lagging UI update issue seems to associated with React's "state snap-shot" and "batch rendering" feature ("double-click to render commits"). This "lagging UI" issue occurs when you put a 'state variable' inside another state setter function, so a solution is to place the actual values that update that 'state variable's state setter function' inside that "outer" state setter function.

ex.
function getGratuityPercentage (value) {
   setGratuityTotal (subTotal * (Gratuity / 100)) ==> setGratuityTotal (subTotal * (value / 100));
   setFinalPrice (subTotal + GratuityTotal + taxedTotal) ==> setFinalPrice(subTotal + subTotal * (value / 100) + taxedTotal)
}

